## ⚠️ High Priority Security Issues

### 6. **Overly Permissive CORS in Production** - [index.ts:52-60](file:///c:/Users/ayush.nalawade/Downloads/veggies_fresh-master/veggies_backend/src/index.ts#L52-L60)

**Severity:** HIGH  
**Impact:** Allows any localhost/192.168.x IP, vulnerable to CSRF attacks

```typescript
if (origin.includes('localhost') || 
    origin.includes('127.0.0.1') || 
    origin.includes('192.168.') || 
    origin.includes('10.0.2.2')) {
  callback(null, true);
}
```

**Issue:** This permissive CORS will work in production based on NODE_ENV check. Allows any local network origin.

**Recommendation:** Use strict whitelist in production, environment-based configuration.

---

### 7. **Password Storage Uses bcrypt (Good!) But Missing Password Complexity Validation**

**Severity:** MEDIUM  
**Current:** Minimum 6 characters only

**Recommendation:** Add password strength requirements:
- Minimum 8 characters
- At least one uppercase, lowercase, number
- Consider adding password strength meter

---

### 8. **No Rate Limiting on Critical Endpoints** - [index.ts:77](file:///c:/Users/ayush.nalawade/Downloads/veggies_fresh-master/veggies_backend/src/index.ts#L77)

**Severity:** HIGH  
**Impact:** Vulnerable to brute force and DDoS attacks

```typescript
app.use('/auth', limiter); // Only auth routes protected
```

**Issue:** Checkout, cart, and order endpoints have no rate limiting.

**Fix Required:** Add rate limiting to `/checkout`, `/cart`, and other sensitive endpoints.

---

### 9. **JWT Token in URL Query Parameters** - [auth.ts:239](file:///c:/Users/ayush.nalawade/Downloads/veggies_fresh-master/veggies_backend/src/controllers/auth.ts#L239)

**Severity:** MEDIUM  
**Impact:** Tokens logged in browser history and server logs

```typescript
const { code } = req.query; // OAuth callback
```

**Current Implementation:** While not directly exposing JWT in query, OAuth flow could be improved.

---

### 10. **No Request ID Tracking**

**Severity:** MEDIUM  
**Impact:** Difficult to trace requests through logs for debugging

**Recommendation:** Add middleware to generate and track request IDs.

